SP-062 complete.

- Step 1: `cli/cmd/stet/capture_test.go` — `captureOutput(t, fn)` creates both pipes, swaps `os.Stdout`/`os.Stderr`, drains each read end in a goroutine while `fn` runs, restores originals via `defer` (covers t.Fatal/panic), closes all four pipe ends; documented as unsafe for parallel tests. Helper tests: 160 KiB (>128 KiB) stdout completes without hanging, streams captured separately, streams restored (incl. after panic). `runCLICapture` rewritten on the helper (signature and `getFindingsOut` handling unchanged).
- Step 2: All 36 remaining `os.Pipe()` sites in `main_test.go` migrated (34 tests + `runCLIWithOutput`, which now takes `t` — 16 call sites updated). Assertions unchanged. Notable fix during the work: the helper's return values were initially snapshotted before `drains.Wait()` (plain `return` evaluates before deferred cleanup) — fixed with named returns assigned after drains finish.
- Step 3: Contract `testCommand` green (gofmt OK, `go vet ./cli/...` OK, `go test ./cli/cmd/stet/... -count=1 -cover` OK). Coverage 74.4% before = 74.4% after. `rg -n 'os\.Pipe\(\)' cli/cmd/stet/main_test.go` returns nothing; `os.Pipe()` only in `cli/cmd/stet/capture_test.go`. Extra `-race` sanity runs pass.

Scope: only `cli/cmd/stet/capture_test.go` (new) and `cli/cmd/stet/main_test.go` changed. No production code touched. `TestRunCLI_skillPrintsToStdout` lost its `t.Parallel()` (required by the helper's no-parallel contract; assertions unchanged) — logged in STATUS.md Discoveries along with out-of-scope `os.Pipe()` uses in `cli/internal/*` tests.
